{"id": "9b720a9f9e9871a016a0de5aed8e7f77e56468f55739feb33698b290a15e48c4", "source": "manual", "feed_url": "inputs/korea", "title": "South Korea  Foreign Trade   Moody's Analytics Economic View", "url": "", "published_at": null, "fetched_at": "2026-02-07T20:39:44Z", "summary": "PDF text extraction is low-quality; please add a manual summary in a .md file with the same base name.", "body": "Dave Chia\nActual US$8.7 bil\nPrevious * US$12.2 bil\nCoverage Jan. 2026\nNext ReleaseMar 01, 2026\nUpdated Jan 31, 2026\nDefinition Source\nFirst Take\nSouth Korea delivered a strong trade performance in January, with the surplus remaining\nhigh at $8.7 billion despite easing from $12.2 billion in December. Exports surged 33.9%\nyear on year, supported by more working days versus a year earlier and solid\nsemiconductor shipments. Imports rose 11.7%. We expect export growth to stay robust in\nearly 2026 on the back of sustained semiconductor demand, although U.S. tariff risks and\nbroader global trade frictions warrant close monitoring.\n\n\nSouth Korea Foreign Trade, US$ mil\n Jan 26 Dec 25 Nov 25 Oct 25 Sep 25 Aug 25 Jul 25\nTrade Balance 8,700 12,170 9,489 6,017 9,499 6,419 6,536\n Exports 65,900 69,539 60,769 59,517 65,908 58,272 60,727\n Imports 57,100 57,368 51,280 53,500 56,408 51,853 54,191\n% change yr ago        \n Exports 33.9 13.3 8.0 3.5 12.6 1.1 5.7\n Imports 11.7 4.6 1.1 -1.5 8.3 -4.1 0.7\n Customize this chart\nIndicators\nForeign Trade\nSouth Korea\n Jan 31, 2026\nDate Published\n\nThe Numbers\nSouth Korea posted a trade surplus of $8.7 billion in January. Exports had their\nstrongest ever January, thanks to more working days and robust semiconductor\ndemand.\nExports rose 33.9% y/y after rising 13.3% in December. Imports climbed 11.7% after\nrising 4.6% in the prior month.\nAcross major export categories, a 102.7% year-on-year jump in semiconductors was\nnoteworthy. Automobiles, another key export category, rose 21.7%. Machinery rose\n8.6%, but petrochemicals dropped 1.5%.\nExports to major trading partners rose, including to China (up 46.7%), the U.S. (up\n29.5%), the EU27 (up 6.9%), and to ASEAN (up 40.7%).\nBehind the Numbers\nSouth Korea started 2026 on a solid footing, recording its 12th consecutive monthly trade\nsurplus in January. That said, the headline strength should not be interpreted as a strong\nturnaround. Januaryʼs strong export print was amplified by favourable calendar effects in\na month that typically sees softer performances. This helped exports post their strongest\nJanuary growth and extend their expansion to an eighth consecutive month.\nSemiconductors were again the linchpin of the trade performance, with artificial\nintelligence-related demand buoying shipments of advanced chips. While automobiles\nand other manufactured goods also registered gains, momentum outside semiconductors\nwas uneven. These sectors face a 15% U.S. tariff burden, which constrains\ncompetitiveness. We expect export growth to carry through the early months of 2026.\nRobust semiconductor demand will provide support amid limited gains in other\nsegments.\nTrade policy risks are elevated. The October U.S.–South Korea trade agreement lowering\nU.S. auto tariffs to 15% from 25% provides partial relief, but the burden remains\nsubstantial given South Koreaʼs heavy reliance on U.S.-bound shipments. U.S. President\nDonald Trump last week threatened to raise tariffs back to 25%, underscoring political\nand policy uncertainty. The threat appeared to be more about pressuring Seoul to\naccelerate legislative approval of the 2025 trade agreement than signalling a breakdown in\nbilateral ties.\n\nExports to China and the U.S. declined in 2025. Favourable base effects flattered gains in\nother major markets. Although the trade surplus highlights South Koreaʼs external\nresilience, rising protectionism and slowing global demand warrant caution.\nSemiconductor demand, the durability of trade agreements, and volatile global conditions\nwill determine South Korea's trade trajectory in 2026.", "tags": ["manual", "korea", "pdf"], "attachment_path": "inputs/korea/pdf/South Korea_ Foreign Trade _ Moody's Analytics Economic View.pdf", "readability_score": 0.6660913140311804, "summary_scaffold_path": "inputs/korea/pdf/South Korea_ Foreign Trade _ Moody's Analytics Economic View.md", "summary_scaffold_created": true}
